This product includes software developed by third parties:

* maunium.net/go/mautrix (MPL-2.0) — the Matrix client and appservice library,
  and the bridgev2 framework that provides the portals, ghosts and message
  plumbing for the messaging half of the bridge.
* go.mau.fi/util (MPL-2.0) — database, config-upgrade and pointer helpers used
  alongside bridgev2.
* github.com/golang-jwt/jwt/v5 (MIT) — signs the short-lived LiveKit access
  tokens the twirp SIP calls are authenticated with.
* github.com/rs/zerolog (MIT) — structured logging, the logger type bridgev2
  hands to network connectors.

Transitively, the build also links (all via mautrix and go.mau.fi/util):

* github.com/lib/pq (MIT) — PostgreSQL driver.
* github.com/mattn/go-sqlite3 (MIT) — SQLite driver, required by bridgev2's
  mxmain even when PostgreSQL is used.
* github.com/coder/websocket (ISC) — appservice websocket transport.
* github.com/yuin/goldmark (MIT) — Markdown to HTML for Matrix message bodies.
* github.com/tidwall/gjson, match, pretty, sjson (MIT) — JSON manipulation.
* filippo.io/edwards25519 (BSD-3-Clause) — Ed25519 arithmetic for the pure-Go
  Olm implementation.
* golang.org/x/crypto, exp, net, sync, sys, text (BSD-3-Clause) — Go extended
  standard library.
* github.com/rs/xid (MIT), github.com/mattn/go-colorable (MIT),
  github.com/mattn/go-isatty (MIT), github.com/coreos/go-systemd/v22
  (Apache-2.0), github.com/petermattis/goid (Apache-2.0),
  github.com/pkg/errors (BSD-2-Clause), github.com/skip2/go-qrcode (MIT),
  go.mau.fi/zeroconfig (MPL-2.0), gopkg.in/yaml.v3 (MIT and Apache-2.0),
  gopkg.in/natefinch/lumberjack.v2 (MIT) — logging, configuration and
  miscellaneous support.

The bridge's connector package began as a copy of the mautrix-twilio skeleton
(github.com/mautrix/twilio, MPL-2.0), which is the same shape: phone-number
portals, no contact list, no history.
